posts.body:
@BarbieDoll
Hi! Yes, I think it also has to do with it being easier holding my baby on that side. I did tried to make him feed on the other side but not too many times. Plus, he got so used to my left side and was struggling with the other. So now, I have uneven breasts, lol.
You're quite lucky though that they still did both sides! I hope that if ever we do decide to have another baby, he or she will take both breasts. I do know a lot know about breastfeeding so I know better than just to give one breast. Haha!
